-<section style="background:var(--navy)"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;padding:3rem 1.5rem"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.9rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:.8rem">Talk to a licensed Grand Strand agent.</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.6);max-width:560px;margin:0 auto 1.6rem;line-height:1.7">Get straight answers on pricing, neighborhoods, and the financing that fits, from a licensed local agent.</p><div style="display:flex;gap:.75rem;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Speak to a Licensed Agent</a></div></div></section><footer>
+<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/">Buyers</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Second Home</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Second homes</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Where should you buy a second home near Myrtle Beach?<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">Six beach towns, from Cherry Grove to Pawleys Island.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated October 26, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Six beach towns, their rental rules and the yearly tax on a second home.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The beach towns differ most in one thing: whether you may rent your place by the night when you are away. North Myrtle Beach allows it with a city license. The City of Myrtle Beach and Surfside Beach allow it only in some zones. Property tax on a $400,000 second home is about $4,800 to $6,100 a year, three to four times a full-time owner's bill.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="choose"><div class="wrap"><style id="c3-glass">main#main{--g-ink:#8a5226;--g-ink-lg:#a8612c;--g-edge:rgba(255,255,255,.8);--g-hi:inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.95);--g-sh:0 1px 2px rgba(28,32,40,.05),0 14px 36px -20px rgba(28,32,40,.3);--g-r:20px;--g-blur:saturate(150%) blur(16px);background-color:#f8f4ee;background-image:radial-gradient(4